      "start": 1700,
      "details": "<p>\"...In A\u017fia Minor the religion is the \u017fame as in Turky in Europe, where only Mahometani\u017fm is e\u017ftabli\u017fhed, and Chri\u017ftianity of all denominations and Judai\u017fm are barely tolerated ; \u017fo that the patriarchs, archbi\u017fhops, and bi\u017fhops, whether Greeks or Armenians, as well as their \u017fees, churches, and congregations, are not only kept under a \u017ftate of deplorable poverty and \u017fervitude, but tho\u017fe prelates are depo\u017fed, changed, promoted, or oppre\u017f\u017fed, at the will of the \u017fultan and his mini\u017fters.</p>\r\n<p>The principal Greek patriarchs, be\u017fides that of Con\u017ftantinople, are tho\u017fe of Jeru\u017falem, Alexandria, and Antioch. The Armenians have only two of them ; the fir\u017ft re\u017fiding at Ecme\u017fan, a mona\u017ftery in Georgia, and the other at Sis, in Aladulia. Be\u017fides the\u017fe the Ne\u017ftorians are allowed one, whose re\u017fidence is commonly at Mo\u017f\u017ful, in the province of Diarbeckr.</p>\r\n<p>The archbi\u017fhops belonging to the Greeks are Heraclea, Saloniki, Athens, Malva\u017fia, Amphipolis, Neapoli di Romania, Lari\u017f\u017fa, Adrianople, Corinth, Nico\u017fia, Janna, Monemba\u017fia, ...(?), Phanarion, Patras, Procone\u017f\u017fus, Ama\u017fia, ...(?), Tyre, Tyana, and Berytus...\"</p>",
